{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0CL4", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-closed-immersion-proper}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9565c12fca2077134a8b4516b29854c698b338ef393e44c998d577ae71ba02da", "source_text": "A closed immersion of algebraic stacks is a proper morphism of\nalgebraic stacks.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:548d57ade0f4e3f5026b6d3c3589bddc1cb95b430bafeb3dfd15e3922761758c", "unit_id": "tag:0CL8:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0CL4", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{stacks-properties-definition-immersion}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{stacks-properties-section-properties-morphisms}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-lemma-closed-immersion-proper}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:18208ecad82bfcf05a5cf9b134a370e6adbd773bdf1ac43d653a83c6b18e2eb6", "source_text": "A closed immersion is by definition representable\n(Properties of Stacks, Definition\n<REF_0001>).\nHence this follows from the discussion in\nProperties of Stacks, Section\n<REF_0002>\nand the corresponding result for morphisms of algebraic spaces, see\nMorphisms of Spaces, Lemma\n<REF_0003>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ca3f70c92e191a1911bb588313aa45ec417d38682dedc35c69b3c8826fcf61b8", "unit_id": "tag:0CL8:proof"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0CL4", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\mathcal{X} \\ar[rr] \\ar[rd] & &\n\\mathcal{Y} \\ar[ld] \\\\\n& \\mathcal{Z} &\n}\n$$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{Y} \\to \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0005": "$|\\mathcal{X}|$", "MATH_0006": "$|\\mathcal{Y}|$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{Y} \\to \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-universally-closed-permanence}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:973a5966005b2946e4fe619d313847694461fc6067b76b1b933492f8c36193fa", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2cf9a64b8149145a2b7d1aa34c0d6bf42bec6d6d7ebde627e3c425fe6224d72c", "source_text": "Consider a commutative diagram\n<MATH_0001>\nof algebraic stacks.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> If <MATH_0002> is universally closed and\n<MATH_0003> is separated,\nthen the morphism <MATH_0004> is universally closed.\nIn particular, the image of <MATH_0005> in <MATH_0006> is closed.\n<STRUCT_0003> If <MATH_0007> is proper and\n<MATH_0008> is separated, then\nthe morphism <MATH_0009> is proper.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:cbf9707c78d2b358af648b77923a6effd2ae8e24b34a5baf16dce12759754894", "unit_id": "tag:0CPT:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0CL4", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{Y} \\to \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{X} \\times_\\mathcal{Z} \\mathcal{Y} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{X} \\times_\\mathcal{Z} \\mathcal{Y} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-semi-diagonal}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-base-change-universally-closed}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-composition-universally-closed}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-compose-after-separated}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{lemma-quasi-compact-permanence}", "REF_0006": "\\ref{lemma-finite-type-permanence}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:be54a7ac28d3608421a98cfc73c4c4582959c20f21a2d516b3aa8123b68b1061", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e38c2d1a61192ff059a741e75e24b4d737cb5bc1115b90825065bdf8a5f43c77", "source_text": "Assume <MATH_0001> is universally closed and\n<MATH_0002> is separated.\nWe factor the morphism as\n<MATH_0003>.\nThe first morphism is proper (Lemma <REF_0001>)\nhence universally closed.\nThe projection <MATH_0004>\nis the base change of a universally closed morphism and hence\nuniversally closed, see\nLemma <REF_0002>.\nThus <MATH_0005> is universally closed as the composition\nof universally closed morphisms, see\nLemma <REF_0003>.\nThis proves (1). To deduce (2) combine (1) with\nLemmas <REF_0004>,\n<REF_0005>, and\n<REF_0006>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ecdd928c6c7c0b2ec8674bb4ef670c698d4e480542a9576cbc2a87e9e56a1920", "unit_id": "tag:0CPT:proof"}
